<title>TURKEY: Turkey's Koc to take five pct stake in Uzbek firm.</title>
<headline>Turkey's Koc to take five pct stake in Uzbek firm.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's industrial conglomerate Koc Holding AS said on Wednesday it planned to take a five percent stake in a company to produce buses and vans in Samarkant, Uzbekistan.</p>
<p>Koc said in a statement to Istanbul Stock Exchange that the firm Samkocauto would have a capital of $27.5 million.</p>
<p>Koc's subsidiaries, Ram Dis Ticaret and Kofisa Trading Co, based in Switzerland, also planned to take up stakes in the firm of 16 percent and 30 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>The Uzbek firm Uzautosanoat will have a 49 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
